# DIAGNOSTICS

Fewer than two arguments or an unknown flag prints the usage message and exits 1.
With more than two arguments and a <dest> that is not a directory it says `cp: /x: not a directory` and exits 1.
A <source> that cannot be copied is reported, as `cp: stat /x: No such file or directory` or `cp: /d is a directory`, and the rest are copied; the exit status is then 1.

# BUGS

A <source> and <dest> that are the same file are reported as `same file` and skipped, but the exit status stays 0.

With `-a`, a device, FIFO or socket is made with `mknod`, which the C library does not implement on VectraOS, so it fails with `Function not implemented`.
With `-p` or `-a`, whether the owner and group can be set depends on the file server; a failure is reported and the exit status is 1.
Neither is tested on VectraOS.

Hard links are not kept: each name of a file is copied as a file of its own.
